                                                                                              <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/Claim> ;
                                                                                     rdfs:label "If expressivists can assert everything realists assert, the dispute between them loses substantive content."@en .


###  http://www.github.com/silvialx/Onto/IfGoodMeantThatPropertyAnalyticallyTheQuestionWouldBeTrivialOrClosed
ex:IfGoodMeantThatPropertyAnalyticallyTheQuestionWouldBeTrivialOrClosed rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                 <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/Claim> ;
                                                                        rdfs:label "If 'good' meant that natural property analytically, the question of whether something with it is good would be trivial or closed, not open."@en .


###  http://www.github.com/silvialx/Onto/IfThatConnectionIsMerelyContingentItIsPuzzlingWhyMoralityShouldBeAuthoritative
ex:IfThatConnectionIsMerelyContingentItIsPuzzlingWhyMoralityShouldBeAuthoritative rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                           <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/Claim> ;
                                                                                  rdfs:label "If the connection between moral judgment and motivation is merely contingent, it becomes puzzling why moral considerations should be practically authoritative at all."@en .


###  http://www.github.com/silvialx/Onto/InternalismBetterExplainsThePracticalAuthorityOfMoralRequirements
ex:InternalismBetterExplainsThePracticalAuthorityOfMoralRequirements rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                              <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/Claim> ;
