                     ex:metaphysicalSupposition ex:Antirealist ;
                     ex:representationSupposition ex:Representationalist ;
                     ex:truthAptnessSupposition ex:TruthApt ;
                     rdfs:comment "moral discourse is a useful fiction: moral sentences are genuinely truth-apt and, taken at face value, are typically false (there being no moral facts), but we are nonetheless warranted in continuing to engage in the practice as one engages with a fiction (Joyce)." .


