ex:ReductiveNaturalism rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                ex:ConsistentPosition ,
                                ex:MetaethicalPosition ;
                       ex:cognitivistSupposition ex:Cognitivist ;
                       ex:epistemicSupposition ex:Empiricist ;
                       ex:metaphysicalSupposition ex:NaturalRealism ;
                       ex:representationSupposition ex:Representationalist ;
                       ex:truthAptnessSupposition ex:TruthApt ;
                       rdfs:comment "moral terms are synonymous with, or analytically reducible to, some set of natural (e.g. psychological or sociological) terms (the classical naturalism Moore's Open Question Argument targets)." .


###  http://www.github.com/silvialx/Onto/ReflectionDestroysKnowledge
ex:ReflectionDestroysKnowledge rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                        <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/Argument> ;
                               <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/hasPremise> :CultureAndEthicalKnowledge ;
                               <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/supports> ex:Relativism ;
                               rdfs:label "Of we accept that there can be ethical knowledge within a culture without comparing the culture one belongs to with another, and if we accept the obvious truth that reflection characteristially disturbs, unseats, or replace those traditional concepts, then we reach the notably un-Socratic conclusion that, in ethics, reflection can destroy knowledge." .


###  http://www.github.com/silvialx/Onto/ReflectiveEquilibrium
ex:ReflectiveEquilibrium rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                  <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/Claim> ;
                         rdfs:label "Moral reasoning is a process that begins with moral presuppositions and proceeds by negotiating conflicting presuppositions. This process is what \"constructs\" complex, individual or social, moral or ethical systems." .


###  http://www.github.com/silvialx/Onto/ReflectiveEquilibriumist
ex:ReflectiveEquilibriumist rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                     ex:Epistemology ;
                            ex:isConditionallyCompatibleWith ex:Coherentist ,
                                                             ex:Intuitionist ;
                            ex:isIncompatibleWith ex:Empiricist ,
                                                  ex:Fictionalist ,
                                                  ex:Skeptic ;
                            skos:definition "moral knowledge (or warranted moral belief) results from a Rawlsian process of mutually adjusting general principles and particular judgments until they cohere." .


###  http://www.github.com/silvialx/Onto/Relativism
ex:Relativism rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       ex:ConsistentPosition ,
                       ex:MetaethicalPosition ;
              ex:actionMotivationSupposition ex:Internalist ;
              ex:cognitivistSupposition ex:Cognitivist ;
              ex:epistemicSupposition ex:Coherentist ;
              ex:metaphysicalSupposition ex:Relativist ;
              ex:representationSupposition ex:Representationalist ;
              ex:truthAptnessSupposition ex:TruthApt ;
              rdfs:comment "moral claims are true or false only relative to the standards of a given moral framework; 'ought' functions like an inherently relational, agreement-relative predicate (Harman's relativism about moral 'oughts')." .


