                                      ex:Realist ;
                skos:definition "Subjectivism holds that moral properties are reducible to, or constituted by, the attitudes of individual subjects (actual or idealized)." .


###  http://www.github.com/silvialx/Onto/SupervenienceArgument
ex:SupervenienceArgument rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                  <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/Argument> ;
                         <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/hasConclusion> ex:ExpressivismExplainsMoralSupervenienceMoreCheaplyThanNonNaturalism ;
                         <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/hasPremise> ex:AProjectivistStoryExplainsWhyWeTreatEvaluativeAndDescriptiveJudgmentsAsBound ,
                                                                              ex:MoralPropertiesNecessarilySuperveneOnNaturalProperties ,
                                                                              ex:NonNaturalismLeavesThisNecessaryConnectionMysterious ;
                         <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/negates> ex:NonReductiveNaturalism ,
                                                                           ex:Nonnaturalism ;
                         <http://www.github.com/argumentsontology/supports> ex:BlackburnExpressivism ;
                         rdfs:label "moral properties necessarily supervene on natural ones, yet this necessary connection is left mysterious by non-naturalism; a projectivist/expressivist story about why we treat evaluative and descriptive judgments as bound together explains the supervenience more cheaply (Blackburn)." .


###  http://www.github.com/silvialx/Onto/TheExpressivistRealistDisputeBecomesMerelyVerbalOrTrivial
